# CHANGELOG.md is append-only under `## [Unreleased]`, and AGENTS.md requires
# every PR to add an entry there. Two PRs adding different bullets is therefore
# not a real conflict, but git stops on it anyway. `union` keeps both sides.
#
# Two failure modes to know about, because union NEVER reports a conflict for
# this file and so never asks you to look:
#
#   1. It is line-based, not section-aware, so a bullet can land under an
#      adjacent heading.
#   2. If two branches edit the SAME entry, union keeps BOTH versions rather
#      than conflicting. You get a duplicated, contradictory bullet. Verified:
#      two branches editing one line merge silently into two lines.
#
# So the `## [Unreleased]` block needs one skim per release. See RELEASING.md.
# GitHub does not read this file, so its own merge and squash-conflict detection
# are unaffected; this helps the local `git merge origin/main`.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
